############ CONFIG MAPS & SECRETS ################

COnfig maps stores data or app vars which are not sesnitive 
NOTE:- Config maps can also be mount to pod/deployment as a Volume

SECRETS:- Secrets stores sensitive app vars such as DB password etc.
_______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________ 

1. StorageClass

In AKS, you typically use the built-in StorageClass. For learning purposes:

apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: StorageClass
metadata:
  name: managed-premium
provisioner: disk.csi.azure.com
parameters:
  skuName: Premium_LRS
reclaimPolicy: Delete
volumeBindingMode: WaitForFirstConsumer
allowVolumeExpansion: true
2. PersistentVolume

Normally AKS creates this automatically when using dynamic provisioning, but here's an example of a manually-created PV:

apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolume
metadata:
  name: app-pv
spec:
  capacity:
    storage: 5Gi
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  storageClassName: managed-premium
  hostPath:
    path: /data/app

Note: hostPath is only for learning/testing. In AKS production environments, Azure Disks are typically provisioned dynamically.

3. PersistentVolumeClaim

The application requests storage through a PVC.

apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: app-pvc
spec:
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  storageClassName: managed-premium
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 5Gi

Binding:

app-pvc  --->  app-pv
4. ConfigMap

Application configuration.

apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: app-config
data:
  APP_ENV: production
  LOG_LEVEL: INFO
  DB_HOST: mysql-service
5. Secret

Sensitive values.

apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: app-secret
type: Opaque
stringData:
  DB_USERNAME: admin
  DB_PASSWORD: SuperSecretPassword
6. Pod

This Pod consumes everything:

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: demo-app
spec:
  containers:
  - name: app
    image: nginx

    env:
    - name: APP_ENV
      valueFrom:
        configMapKeyRef:
          name: app-config
          key: APP_ENV

    - name: LOG_LEVEL
      valueFrom:
        configMapKeyRef:
          name: app-config
          key: LOG_LEVEL

    - name: DB_HOST
      valueFrom:
        configMapKeyRef:
          name: app-config
          key: DB_HOST

    - name: DB_USERNAME
      valueFrom:
        secretKeyRef:
          name: app-secret
          key: DB_USERNAME

    - name: DB_PASSWORD
      valueFrom:
        secretKeyRef:
          name: app-secret
          key: DB_PASSWORD

    volumeMounts:
    - name: app-storage
      mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html/data
volumes:
  - name: app-storage
    persistentVolumeClaim:
      claimName: app-pvc


